orting the petrol tax increase, this House urges the government to reconsider its unfair budget, including the proposal to raise $10 billion in revenue by removing the fuel tax credit for miners but keeping it for farmers. Bronwyn Bishop I take it the member was seeking leave? Adam Bandt I did seek leave. Bronwyn Bishop Is leave granted? Christopher Pyne Leave is not granted. Adam Bandt I move: That so much of standing and sessional orders be suspended as would prevent the member for Melbourne from moving the following: That in light of reports that government Members of Parliament have been tricked into supporting the petrol tax increase, this House urges the Government to reconsider its unfair Budget, including the proposal to raise $10 billion in revenue by removing the fuel tax credit for miners, but keeping it for farmers. People in the gallery and members of the public might be listening to this and may be surprised to know— Christopher Pyne Madam Speaker, on a point of order: I move: That member be no longer heard. _A division having been called and the bells being rung—_ Mr Fitzgibbon interjecting— Bronwyn Bishop I think that interjection is almost worthy of having to wear a bowler hat on your head to ask the question. The question is that the member be no longer heard.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-3215","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2014-06-05/2"}
